From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: coremessaging: Windows.System.DispatcherQueue

CreateDispatcherQueueController was E_NOTIMPL, so every program built on
DispatcherQueue -- WinUI 3 / Windows App SDK programs, Paint.NET 5 and its
installer -- stopped at its first line.

A DispatcherQueue runs work items, by priority (high, normal, low; first
in, first out within one), on one thread's message loop: the calling
thread's (DQTYPE_THREAD_CURRENT) or a thread of its own
(DQTYPE_THREAD_DEDICATED, DispatcherQueueController.CreateOnDedicatedThread;
COM STA when asked). Each queue has a message-only window on its thread:
TryEnqueue posts to it from any thread, DispatcherQueueTimer is its
WM_TIMERs, and ShutdownQueueAsync is a message too -- ShutdownStarting,
the queued work, ShutdownCompleted, then its IAsyncAction completes and no
more work is taken. HasThreadAccess, DispatcherQueue.GetForCurrentThread,
one queue per thread. Written from the public API documentation.

Not done: ShutdownStarting's deferrals are not waited for.

Gate: test/dispatcherq-gate.sh.
