+/*
+ * Windows.System.DispatcherQueue: a queue of work items run, in priority
+ * order, by one thread's message loop -- the calling thread's
+ * (DQTYPE_THREAD_CURRENT, which must pump messages) or a thread of its own
+ * (DQTYPE_THREAD_DEDICATED, DispatcherQueueController.CreateOnDedicatedThread).
+ * Each queue has a message-only window on its thread: enqueueing posts to
+ * it, timers are its WM_TIMERs, and shutting down is a message too, so the
+ * handlers always run on the queue's thread.
+ */
+
